# Design and planning documents. These drive the work but are not part of the shipped project,
# and they are large enough to bury real changes in a diff. They stay on disk; git ignores them.
#
# `design/design-tokens.py` is deliberately NOT here: it is a build tool, not a document. It
# generates the palette and `packages/web/src/styles/tokens.css` via `pnpm tokens:css`, and CI
# fails if the committed CSS does not match what it emits.
CLAUDE.md
PRD.md
TECH-DESIGN.md
design/DESIGN-BRIEF.md
design/CLAUDE-DESIGN-PROMPT.md
